Project-Specific Information
KLJ
KU has reviewed the information in Exhibit A of the RFP including the operations overview and background of the project, and
understand that the landfill is broken into two phases with the focus of the REP being on Phase 1 for the fill areas that will need
to be clearly defined in any maps or grid plans produced.
We are also aware of the survey points that may be available for use in our site work and, if available, will work with the staff to
identify the location of them as needed.
We understand that a Wyoming Licensed Land Surveyor is required to oversee the field tasks listed in Section 2 of the RFP and
will generate the grid plans, as required, up to three, for the permitted area to be used on-site. In conjunction with this, KU
understands that up to three site visits may be requested for each year of the contract.
Upon the second mapping survey of the site, SWT will coordinate with KU to produce the AUF report and lsopach as requested
in task 2 of Section 2 of the RFP and will submit for City approval prior to finalizing.
